# src/multiplyTwoNumbers.asm is committed with CRLF line endings. Unsetting the
# text attribute disables end-of-line conversion for it entirely, so no
# contributor's core.autocrlf setting can renormalize the file and turn a
# one-line change into a whole-file diff.
#
# Note: `*.asm text eol=crlf` would NOT be equivalent -- it stores LF in the
# index, which is the very renormalization this line exists to prevent.
*.asm -text
